# Keep VCS metadata and dev/CI files out of the Docker build context so a COPY can
# never sweep credentials into an image layer. This is defense-in-depth: an
# actions/checkout .git/config persists its token as an http.extraheader, and a
# broad COPY of a checkout dir would otherwise bake that token into a published layer.
#
# Do NOT ignore files the Dockerfiles COPY from context:
#   - THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md      (Dockerfile.relion)
#   - extras/ctffind-*.tar.gz      (Dockerfile.relion)

.git
.gitattributes
.github
.dockerignore

client/
extras/Dockerfile.*

CHANGELOG.md
CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
README.md
SECURITY.md
release-please.config.json
.release-please.manifest.json
